# Cloudflare Workers secrets for LOCAL DEV ONLY. Copy this file to `.dev.vars`
# (gitignored) and fill in real values — `wrangler`/`astro dev` reads secrets
# from `.dev.vars`, not from `.env` (Vite's `.env` only covers PUBLIC_-
# prefixed, build-time-inlined variables; these are runtime Worker secrets,
# read via `import { env } from "cloudflare:workers"`).
#
# In production, set the same names with:
#   npx wrangler secret put MSFT_TENANT_ID
#   npx wrangler secret put MSFT_GSA_CLIENT_ID
#   npx wrangler secret put MSFT_GSA_CLIENT_SECRET
# (or via the Cloudflare dashboard's Worker > Settings > Variables page).
#
# Leave these unset (locally or in production) to keep using the built-in
# mock Microsoft Global Secure Access provider — src/lib/providers/microsoft-gsa.ts
# falls back to it automatically when credentials aren't configured.
#
# Requires an Entra ID app registration with the NetworkAccess.Read.All
# APPLICATION permission (admin-consented), and a tenant with Global Secure
# Access / Entra Internet Access web content filtering enabled.
MSFT_TENANT_ID=
MSFT_GSA_CLIENT_ID=
MSFT_GSA_CLIENT_SECRET=
